{"tool_name":"conics","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"conics","home":"https://github.com/diazlab/CONICS","summary":"Integrates scRNA-seq with DNA sequencing to map gene expression to tumor sub-clones.","addition_date":"2018-06-01T15:54:41Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:36:34.970320Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:conics","credit":[{"email":"aaron.diaz@ucsf.edu","name":"Aaron Diaz","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/diazlab/CONICS"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Copy number estimation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3233"},{"term":"DNA mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2520"}]}],"name":"CONICS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty316","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Single-cell RNA-sequencing (scRNA-seq) has enabled studies of tissue composition at unprecedented resolution. However, the application of scRNA-seq to clinical cancer samples has been limited, partly due to a lack of scRNA-seq algorithms that integrate genomic mutation data. Results: To address this, we present CONICS: COpy-Number analysis In single-Cell RNA-Sequencing. CONICS is a software tool for mapping gene expression from scRNA-seq to tumor clones and phylogenies, with routines enabling: the quantitation of copy-number alterations in scRNA-seq, robust separation of neoplastic cells from tumor-infiltrating stroma, inter-clone differential-expression analysis and intra-clone co-expression analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Cho A."},{"name":"Diaz A."},{"name":"Lim D.A."},{"name":"Liu S.J."},{"name":"Muller S."}],"citationCount":58,"date":"2018-09-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"CONICS integrates scRNA-seq with DNA sequencing to map gene expression to tumor sub-clones"},"pmcid":"PM